Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:41:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docs(process): /resolve-conflicts skill and the conflict rule
 in the automation law (PROCESS_VERSION 3)

Merging moves main, so reviewed PRs keep turning `conflicts`; yesterday's
/merge-ready run left 18 of 55 conflicting. Most conflicts are a merge of
main where both sides added lines.

- New project skill .claude/skills/resolve-conflicts:
  - contributor mode (/resolve-conflicts [login]) merges main into the
    author's conflicting PRs, keeps both sides of additive conflicts,
    takes main's snapshot PNGs and changelog files, runs the targeted
    gate, pushes (never rebase/force), comments "ready for a re-check";
    stops and reports when both sides changed the same logic or a safety
    rule could be dropped.
  - maintainer mode (/resolve-conflicts check) re-reads every `conflicts`
    PR: asks the author once if still conflicting; when clean drops the
    label and restores merge-ready, or routes to a delta or full review.
- AGENTS.md Autonomous Work Law: "Conflicted PRs are re-merged by their
  author; the maintainer re-checks", including when forks run it.
- .claude/PROCESS_VERSION 2 -> 3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
